# Run r1103, slice B, boot 2 (sB_2): the same level sb1 as sB_1 (group A superflat), restarted with the 1.0.1 Creative
# Labels build jar back in srv/mods. Setup in sB_setup.md (probes zz_zsb_probe.js, zz_zlbs_probe.js; /zq from prep_srv).
# Order: boot-log and kjsexpect rows first (SQ-CF-02 reads the world's serverconfig written at sB_1's first boot), the
# SQ-LBS-05 old-save compare before any other label row, then /zq and /zsb data rows, block and bot rows, the
# randomTickSpeed row (SQ-VTD9-01), and the /reload row (SQ-CUP-04) last.
#
# Superflat: grass y -61, air from y -60. Areas (forceloaded by the first row): cltest area x -8..170 z -8..16 (sB_1's
# notes and labels, kept), /zlbs hosts x 300..360 z 16..40 at y -58, row lane x 96..212 z 496..512 (one x per row,
# listed in the row). SQ-VTD9-01 forceloads its own lane x 0..200 z 1000..1060. Bots: perfBot, one name per row,
# removed at the end of the row (bots near a lane would give it random ticks).
pace 2

## SQ-CF-02 | Spice of Life world config from defaultconfigs: movement speed attribute (A, new level)
bootexpect Done \(
shell L=$(grep -m1 '^level-name=' server.properties | cut -d= -f2); f="$L/serverconfig/solapplepie-server.toml"; ls -l defaultconfigs/solapplepie-server.toml "$f"; grep -oE "generic\.(movement_)?speed,[0-9.]+" "$f"; grep -nE "minFoodsToActivate|resetOnDeath|queueSize" "$f"; grep -niE "solapplepie" logs/latest.log | grep -iE "warn|error" | head; grep -q "generic.movement_speed,0.01" "$f" && ! grep -q "generic.speed,2" "$f"
bootreject (?i)solapplepie.*(attribute|unknown).*(warn|error|invalid)
# areas for the whole batch; 30 s before any block tick
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
> gamerule doDaylightCycle false
> time set noon
> weather clear 100000
> forceload add -8 -8 170 16
> forceload add 296 16 364 40
> forceload add 96 496 212 512
sleep 30
look rows/SQ-CF-02.shell.txt: generic.movement_speed,0.01 and no generic.speed,2; minFoodsToActivate 10, resetOnDeath true, queueSize 256; no attribute warning (the 4 known largemeals complexity warnings are fine)

## SQ-CUP-01 | Miner's Delight without the copper cup family: data loads, no cup id anywhere
bootexpect Miner's Delight upstream data: \d+ files
bootreject Cup conversions
bootreject (?i)\bminers_delight:(copper|water|milk|powder_snow|beef_stew|onion_soup|[a-z_]+)_cup\b
bootreject (?i)\bdelightful:cactus_soup_cup\b
kjsreject (?i)\bminers_delight:[a-z_]*_cup\b|cactus_soup_cup
shell n=$(grep -oE "Miner's Delight upstream data: [0-9]+" logs/latest.log | grep -oE "[0-9]+$" | head -1); echo "upstream files $n (182 before)"; grep -nE "Unknown item" logs/kubejs/startup.log logs/kubejs/server.log | grep -iE "item_dict|food_dict|tool_dict|stack_sizes|comfort" | head; echo "handler errors: $(grep -c 'Error occurred while handling event' logs/latest.log)"; [ -n "$n" ] && [ "$n" -lt 182 ]
look rows/SQ-CUP-01.shell.txt: no Unknown item line from the dicts, stack_sizes or comfort_nourishment; any handler error line is unrelated to cups

## SQ-FO-01 | food types line, no food_types warning, no new item_dict Missing for a food key
bootexpect \[food types\] \d+ foods in 31 types, \d+ canned sources
bootreject \[food types\].*(no item_dict key|is in both)
shell grep -hoE "\[food types\] [0-9]+ foods in [0-9]+ types, [0-9]+ canned sources" logs/latest.log | head -3; grep -n "\[item_dict\] Missing" logs/kubejs/startup.log | grep -vE "catfish_slice|jei_bucket_|tmted_|rs_" | head; true
look N about 1016 or more and M about 252 in the [food types] line; any item_dict Missing line printed is not a food key

## SQ-FO-05 | egg stacks 64, stack sizes applied
bootexpect \[stack_sizes\] set \d+ stack sizes
bootreject no item_dict key
